WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.770
METE ATAMEL:
Speech-To-Text API can

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:06.330
be used to convert audio
to text in 120 languages.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.850
Let's see how to use
Speech API with C#.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:12.330
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.540
and a service account
exists to make API calls.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.570
Both are explained in the
codelab in the video notes.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.270
In Cloud Shell, let's
create a simple dotnet

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:25.800
console app and add Speech API
NuGet Package to the project.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.970
Open the Code Editor and
navigate to program.cs.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:33.300
We will transcribe an audio file
saved on Google Cloud Storage.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.190
First, reference to
the Speech API library.

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.540
Create a speech client.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.790
Specify Speech
API configuration.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.420
Point to the audio on
Google Cloud Storage.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.080
Call Recognize method.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.310
And finally, print the results.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.640
Let's run the app.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:55.420
There you go.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.750
You just used the Speech-To-Text
API to convert audio to text.

